      "last_updated": "2026-05-12T00:00:00.000000",
      "title_align": "left",
      "section": "Correlation",
      "order": 6,
      "alignment": "left",
      "vertical_alignment": "top",
      "body": "One HeLa cell, imaged first by fluorescence (DAPI, mitochondria, Golgi, lysosomes) and then by FIB-SEM at 5 nm. The EM volume is read in place from the BioImage Archive (EMPIAR-10819), never copied. The fluorescence was registered into it with an affine fitted on the landmarks the authors placed between the two, and is laid over the EM: the Overlay slider fades it, Z moves through the EM and the overlay follows. DAPI and mitochondria show first; Golgi and lysosomes are under Overlay in the settings. Each dot is a landmark within 0.3 um of the shown plane, coloured by how far it lands from its EM partner after the affine; a lasso around some of them narrows the plots and the table. Five landmarks were left out of the fit: their error is the honest one. Data from Krentzel et al., CLEM-Reg, Nature Methods 2025 (S-BIAD4355, S-BSST707).\n",
      "surface": "none",
      "accent": null,
      "logo": null,
      "logo_dark": null,
      "wf_tag": "python/bioimage_demo"
    },
